    "paper_id": "P002",
    "paper_title": "TRIMMED k-MEANS: AN ATTEMPT TO ROBUSTIFY QUANTIZERS",
    "authors_year": "J. A. Cuesta-Albertos, A. Gordaliza and C. Matrán, 1997",
    "research_question": "How to robustify k-means and associated clustering analysis using impartial trimming (self-determined by data) and establish their theoretical existence, characterization, and strong consistency properties?",
    "methods": [
      "Formulation of alpha-trimmed k-means using generalized trimming functions (measurable functions taking values in [0,1]) to handle partial participation of data points",
      "Application of simulated annealing-based algorithms in MATLAB to handle the non-existence of a deterministic optimal algorithm",
      "Sensitivity studies and simulations using bivariate normal mixture distributions contaminated by inner and outer outliers under various configurations of cluster separation, dispersion, and trimming sizes (alpha)"
    ],
    "main_findings": [
      "The best trimming function essentially coincides with the indicator function of a nonpathological set: the union of k balls with the same radius (Corollary 3.2)",
      "Proved the existence of trimmed k-means for continuous, nondecreasing penalty functions satisfying basic conditions (Theorem 3.1)",
      "Established the strong consistency (almost sure convergence in Hausdorff distance of the k-sets and convergence of trimmed k-variations) of empirical trimmed k-means under continuity of the limit distribution (Theorem 3.6)",
      "Simulations demonstrate that trimmed k-means successfully detect anomalous data and estimate cluster means in high-contamination settings, though low trimming levels can introduce estimator bias near dense probability boundaries"
    ],
    "assumptions": [
      "The penalty function Phi is continuous, nondecreasing, with Phi(0) = 0 and Phi(x) < Phi(infinity) for all x",
      "The probability distribution PX of the underlying random vector is continuous (in consistency theorems)",
      "The number of clusters k is specified correctly"
    ],
